name: sim.createShape
description: Creates a mesh shape
luaSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.createShape(int options, float shadingAngle, list vertices, list indices, list normals = None, list textureCoordinates = None, string/bytes texture = None, list textureResolution = None)
pythonSynopsis: int objectHandle = sim.createShape(int options, float shadingAngle, float[] vertices, int[] indices, float[] normals = nil, float[] textureCoordinates = nil, string/buffer texture = nil, int[2] textureResolution = nil)
inputs:
1. options: Bit-coded:
    - if bit0 is set (1), backfaces are culled
    - If bit1 is set (2), edges are visible
    - If bit2 is set (4), adjacent texture pixels are not interpolated
    - If bit3 is set (8), texture is applied as a decal
    - If bit4 is set (16), texture is RGBA, otherwise it is RGB
    - If bit5 is set (32), texture is horizontally flipped
    - If bit6 is set (64), texture is vertically flipped
2. shadingAngle: shading angle
3. vertices: array of vertices
4. indices: array of indices
5. normals: optional array of normal vectors. Has to be 3 * len(indices) in length
6. textureCoordinates: optional array of texture coordinates. Has to be 2 * len(indices) in length
7. texture: optional texture, specified as RGB or RGBA
8. textureResolution: resolution of the specified texture
outputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the newly created shape
replacedBy:
- name: createObject, class: app, file: app_createObject.method
- name: createObject, class: scene, file: scene_createObject.method
